    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171-a2">

                <pb facs="0379" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg359"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Parker.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-11-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 20, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your letter of this date, stating that you
                    are the bearer of an address from the people of Great Britain and Ireland to the
                    people of the United States, has been received. Before answering the question
                    which your letter contains, it is desirable to be further informed whether you
                    have authority from the government of Great Britain and Ireland for the purpose
                    referred to, and whether your mission has been made known to the diplomatic
                    agent of that government accredited to the government of the United States.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your very obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph Parker,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
